From f384098ca2fa95e9f5342c9cd04b9ec58636d9f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:04:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Deskbar: the PROSE mark in place of the Haiku leaf

The Deskbar logo is an HVIF vector icon and the only authoring tool for
that format is Icon-O-Matic, which needs a running Haiku. The mark is
therefore generated by tools/artwork/hvif.py in the HaikuArmQemu repo,
which writes the subset a simple mark needs - solid colour styles and
straight-line paths - following the parser in FlatIconImporter.cpp.

The mark is the same broad-nib sweep as the desktop wallpaper, sampled
from a cubic spine with a pressure profile, so the Deskbar and the
desktop carry the same motif. A first attempt drew a tapered nib and it
came out as a slab: the Deskbar renders the icon into a 63x22 bitmap, so
the 64x64 icon grid is squashed about 3:1 and fine detail does not
survive. One bold stroke does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
